## Dispatch & Routing Layer - main agent orchestrator rules (mandatory)

### Core principles

**Typical routing pattern**: `main agent -> invoke skill -> skill may launch subagent`. Do NOT go deeper (see Crash Prevention).

**Prompt naturalness**: User does NOT say skill/tool names. They state intent/needs/wants/outcomes.
Skill descriptions (already optimized) must match intent automatically.
- **Pro user**: clear intent + context -> match top-1 skill direct, invoke immediately
- **Non-pro user**: vague -> main agent asks 1-2 natural clarifying questions (do NOT list "skill A or B")

### Dispatch Decision Tree

| User intent | Route to |
|---|---|
| Vault/knowledge-base/strategy/OKR/temporal reference ("last week", "decision before") | Skill `vault-research` |
| Code review (general) | Skill `/code-review:code-review` |
| Security/XSS/SQL injection check | Skill `/code-review:security-review` |
| Feature add with codebase exploration | Agent `feature-dev:code-explorer` (built-in) |
| Automation/hook/MCP/plugin dev | Skill `plugin-dev:*` |
| Browser perf/a11y/leak debug | Skill `chrome-devtools-mcp:*` |
| PR/issue/GitHub workflow | Skill `github:*` (slash) |
| Web search/scrape | `WebSearch`/`WebFetch` |
| UI/landing page/component design | Skill `frontend-design` |
| Create skill/agent/plugin | Skill `skill-creator` or `plugin-dev:*` |
| Memory writeback (see threshold below) | `vault-session-end` / `vault-failure-log` / `vault-pattern-extract` / `vault-orchestration-log` |
| Ambiguous (>=3 skill candidates with similar confidence) | Skill `skill-router` (safety net, silent) |
| Coding touching git (any repo) | Phase 0 `repo-capability-discovery` -> wave `multi-subagent-wave-orchestration` |

Plugin capability matrix: `${VAULT_PATH}/Engineering/AI-Memory/agent-profiles/shared-conventions.md` -> "Plugin Capability Matrix".

### Model Tier Matrix

| Tier | When to use | Example tasks | Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Haiku** | Read-only lookup, classification, simple Q&A | Grep, list files, classify intent | Careful: over-caution on write tasks |
| **Sonnet** (default) | Write task, edit, single-file refactor, review | Most everyday tasks | Floor for write tasks |
| **Opus** | Cross-file refactor, orchestration parent, gap analysis | Wave parent, multi-file design | Max 3 concurrent (RAM) |

### Crash Prevention - Agent-Spawn Nesting Rule

The restriction is on **nested SPAWN AGENT depth**, NOT on subagents using skills.
Skills themselves do not count as a tier; only skills that spawn agents create a new tier.

- **Max 2 spawn tiers**: main (tier 0) -> subagent (tier 1) -> subagent (tier 2) is the ceiling.
  Tier 3+ = crash (nested context). Example forbidden chain: main -> subagent -> skill (spawn) -> subagent = tier 3.
- **Subagents MAY invoke appropriate skills** provided the skill does NOT itself spawn a subagent.
- **Skills that launch subagents -> only call from main (tier 0)**, NOT from within a subagent:
  `skill-creator`, `command-development`, `multi-subagent-wave-orchestration`, `/code-review` ultra (cloud fan-out).
- **Unsure if a skill spawns agents -> treat as YES** (fail-safe).
- **Subagent prompt template** MUST include: "May use appropriate skill IF it does not itself spawn a sub-agent; do NOT spawn sub-agents."

### Disambiguation Interaction Pattern

- Pro user prompt with clear intent -> match top-1 -> invoke immediately (no question)
- Non-pro vague -> ask 1-2 natural clarifying questions before routing
- >=3 candidates with similar confidence -> invoke `skill-router` silent (do not ask user "skill A or B")
- **Outcome-first interpretation**: parse intent -> identify outcome -> match skill; do NOT match keyword to tool name

### Memory Writeback Threshold

Invoke log skill when:
- **`vault-session-end`**: >=3 non-trivial tool calls AND outcome produced (file edit, plan, decision)
- **`vault-failure-log`**: failed call needing rework OR same error >=2 times
- **`vault-pattern-extract`**: approach reused >=3 sessions OR explicit user request
- **`vault-orchestration-log`**: multi-wave OR multi-CLI pipeline success
- **Floor**: skip if session <5 min and read-only

