### Git Discipline - Principal Branch Lock (mandatory, every git repo)

- Do NOT `git checkout/switch/commit/rebase/merge/pull/reset --hard` on the principal branch
  (the branch the user is on at start) unless the user explicitly names the branch.
- Task instruction ("fix X", "implement feature Y") != branch instruction.
  Only an explicit branch name is a branch instruction.
- Need different branch state (including new feature) -> `git worktree add` session-scoped path,
  do NOT `git checkout -b` on the principal repo.
- Subagent inherits: prompt must include "DO NOT git checkout/switch/commit unless instructed; use worktree".
- Read-only OK (`git log/diff/status/show/blame`); run `git status --short` + `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD`
  before the first git operation.

